; Field access by name on a `data` type whose constructors do not
; all declare the field. `Shape` has no nullary constructor, so the
; 480 arm does not fire - but `Rect` declares no `r`, and field
; access emits one unguarded load for the name: on a `Rect` value it
; loads the neighbour's slot, and on a shorter block a word past it
; (`check` said OK and the program answered 7, or died of SIGSEGV).
; Only `match` emits the tag guard, so the read is refused in favour
; of one. A field every constructor declares at the same word with
; the same type stays legal.
(data Shape
  (Circle { r : Int })
  (Rect { w : Int, h : Int }))

(:: radius (-> Shape Int))
(fn (radius s) s.r)

(:: main Int)
(fn (main) (radius (Rect 7 9)))
